{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And on the day of your rejoicing and your appointed seasons.</b> When you return from the land of the enemy or defeat the enemy that came against you, and you establish a day of rejoicing like the days of Purim and the seven days of Hezekiah (variant reading: Hanukkah) of rejoicing. Only the copyists explained 'and on the day of your rejoicing' as Shabbat, and the blowing, that Israel hear and know that the burnt offerings are being offered, and direct their heart to HaShem:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase שבעת ימי חזקי\"ה (seven days of Hezekiah) is unusual; the variant reading חנוכה appears in parentheses in the source text, suggesting the scribe or editor noted an alternative tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:01.655736285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}